00:50:56.720 --> 00:50:57.750
As you move up in the company.

00:51:00.020 --> 00:51:07.880
&gt;&gt; You know, It's interesting,
I must say there's many, many dimensions.

00:51:07.880 --> 00:51:11.890
Perhaps the biggest adjustment
was that ability to

00:51:11.890 --> 00:51:16.940
grapple with what is it that uniquely
only you can do, versus what

00:51:16.940 --> 00:51:21.200
others in the team can do getting much
better at it was the most helpful.

00:51:22.500 --> 00:51:28.210
But the CEO job when I look back at it and
many of you, who may,

00:51:28.210 --> 00:51:33.330
start out in, and become even CEOs
much earlier on in your career,

00:51:34.360 --> 00:51:39.870
I had not understood perhaps even growing
up at Microsoft how multi constituent

00:51:39.870 --> 00:51:44.970
the job is right I mean that's perhaps
the biggest adjustment i've had to make.

00:51:44.970 --> 00:51:47.690
Is recognizing, it's about customers,
it's about partners,

00:51:47.690 --> 00:51:52.790
it's about all your employees, it's about
your investors, it's about governments,

00:51:52.790 --> 00:51:55.780
it's about many, many,
many of these constituents.

00:51:55.780 --> 00:52:00.539
And by the way, it's not about, it's not
like office hours for each one of them.

00:52:00.539 --> 00:52:03.220
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; It is about all of them, all.

00:52:03.220 --> 00:52:04.570
All the time.

00:52:04.570 --> 00:52:10.130
And how to think about that
multi-constituent world I think

00:52:10.130 --> 00:52:16.030
is perhaps the biggest adjustment that one
makes as you grow in any organization.

00:52:16.030 --> 00:52:20.198
And the faster you grapple with it,
the better off you will be, and

00:52:20.198 --> 00:52:21.994
your organization will be.

